Five texts. A considered collection.
The Western Canon Set

The Western Canon Set gathers five texts: The Odyssey, The Beatitudes, What i=
s a man profited?, Our heart is restless, and Midway upon the journey.

Homer begins a story of homecoming. Matthew preserves the blessings and the q=
uestion about the soul. Augustine addresses God in prayer. Dante names the da=
rk wood at the beginning of his journey.

These works remain distinct. The source and translation accompany each sheet,=
 so a passage can lead back to the fuller work.

Explore the set for its available formats. The three art reproductions after =
Rembrandt and Blake are offered separately.

Explore the five-sheet set: https://thomasbroadside.co/documents/the-western-=
